---
import '../../styles/ai-guides.css'

import { Alert, Badge, ButtonLink, Code, CodeTabs, Container, Link, Prose, Stack } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import { getGuide } from '../../data/guides'
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const guide = getGuide('/guides/build-an-astro-starter')
const sourceUrl = 'https://github.com/santi020k/lumen/tree/main/examples/astro-starter'

const runExamples = [
  {
    label: 'Downloaded starter',
    value: 'download',
    language: 'bash',
    code: 'unzip lumen-astro-starter.zip\ncd lumen-astro-starter\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm dev'
  },
  {
    label: 'Repository checkout',
    value: 'checkout',
    language: 'bash',
    code: 'git clone https://github.com/santi020k/lumen.git\ncd lumen/examples/astro-starter\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm dev'
  }
] as const

const compositionExample = `---
import { Badge, Card, Stack } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'
---

<Card as="section" aria-labelledby="activity-title">
  <Stack gap="group">
    <h2 id="activity-title">Project activity</h2>
    <p>Your team's latest work, in one place.</p>
    <Badge variant="outline">Updated today</Badge>
  </Stack>
</Card>`
---

<BaseLayout
  article={{ author: guide.author, publishedAt: guide.publishedAt }}
  breadcrumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { href: '/guides', label: 'Guides' }, { href: guide.href, label: guide.title }]}
  description={guide.description}
  title={`${guide.title} — Lumen UI`}
>
  <Container as="main" class="ai-guide" size="md">
    <Stack gap="section">
      <Prose>
        <Badge variant="outline">Free Astro starter · MIT license</Badge>
        <h1>Start with a working screen. Make it yours.</h1>
        <p>
          Build from four editable Lumen templates with a shared theme picker. This walkthrough
          takes you from the live preview to a local project, then through changing the content,
          testing its interactions, and preparing a static build.
        </p>
        <p>By {guide.author} · <time datetime={guide.publishedAt}>November 9, 2026</time></p>
      </Prose>

      <Stack direction="horizontal" gap="related" wrap>
        <ButtonLink href="/starters/astro" showArrow>Explore the starter</ButtonLink>
        <ButtonLink href={sourceUrl} newTab variant="secondary">View source</ButtonLink>
        <ButtonLink href="/downloads/lumen-astro-starter.zip" download variant="secondary">Download ZIP</ButtonLink>
      </Stack>

      <Prose>
        <h2>1. Choose the screen closest to your project</h2>
        <p>
          Open the preview and follow its navigation. Each screen uses public Lumen Astro components,
          so you can copy a composition, adjust its content, and keep using the same component APIs.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><Link href="/starters/astro">Landing page</Link> introduces a product and connects its calls to action to the other templates.</li>
          <li><Link href="/starters/astro/ecommerce">Ecommerce</Link> combines a product collection with an interactive local cart.</li>
          <li><Link href="/starters/astro/dashboard">Dashboard</Link> demonstrates metrics that respond to a reporting period.</li>
          <li><Link href="/starters/astro/portfolio">Portfolio</Link> organizes selected work with category filtering.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Use the theme and appearance controls to compare Lumen, Santi020k, Studio, Paper, Field,
          Glass, and Harbor. Your selection follows you between the starter's pages.
        </p>
      </Prose>

      <Stack as="section" gap="group" aria-labelledby="run-title">
        <Prose>
          <h2 id="run-title">2. Open your own copy</h2>
          <p>
            Download the ZIP or clone the repository to edit your own copy. Use the Node.js and pnpm versions declared
            in the starter's <code>package.json</code>, then run the commands below.
          </p>
        </Prose>
        <CodeTabs ariaLabel="Run the Astro starter locally" items={runExamples} />
        <Prose>
          <p>
            Open the local address printed by Astro. The starter has its own manifest and lockfile,
            so its published Lumen dependencies install independently of the contributor workspace.
            Keep <code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code> when you copy or publish your project.
          </p>
        </Prose>
      </Stack>

      <Stack as="section" gap="group" aria-labelledby="edit-title">
        <Prose>
          <h2 id="edit-title">3. Edit the page you want to keep</h2>
          <p>
            The route files in <code>src/pages/</code> render <code>src/Starter.astro</code>.
            That shared shell owns navigation, theme selection, and the Lumen runtime. Page content lives
            in <code>src/components/Landing.astro</code>, <code>Storefront.astro</code>,
            <code>Dashboard.astro</code>, and <code>Portfolio.astro</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Start with <code>Dashboard.astro</code>. Change its heading to your product's name,
            replace one metric with a representative value, and check each reporting period.
            Keep metric labels, values, and chart data consistent as you replace the sample data.
            Add a small section with public components when you need another content block.
          </p>
        </Prose>
        <Code code={compositionExample} copy label="Compose a dashboard section" language="astro" variant="block" wrap />
        <Prose>
          <p>
            Adjust layout in <code>src/styles/starter.css</code>. Use semantic roles such as
            <code>hsl(var(--surface))</code>, <code>hsl(var(--ink))</code>, and
            <code>hsl(var(--brand))</code> so your additions respond to every theme. Harbor's
            editable example stylesheet is <code>src/styles/harbor.css</code>.
            The shared shell already mounts <code>UIPrimitives</code> once.
          </p>
          <p>
            After you choose the pages for your site, update navigation and remove unused route files.
            Set your final title, description, site URL, and links before deploying.
            Follow the <Link href="/docs/web/themes">web theme guide</Link> when extending the palette.
          </p>
        </Prose>
      </Stack>

      <Stack as="section" gap="group" aria-labelledby="behavior-title">
        <Prose>
          <h2 id="behavior-title">4. Connect your product's data and services</h2>
          <p>
            The cart, reporting periods, and project filters give you concrete interactions to adapt.
            Keep the user-facing states clear while connecting the starter to your application.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>For ecommerce, connect product availability and server-validated prices, then create checkout sessions through your payment provider.</li>
            <li>For a dashboard, load authorized data for the selected date range and show loading, empty, and failed-request states.</li>
            <li>For a portfolio, replace project examples and destinations with your own work and confirm every category has an appropriate result.</li>
          </ul>
        </Prose>
        <Alert>
          The storefront uses sample products and a local cart. Its checkout action displays a demo
          notice. Add your commerce service and payment flow before accepting orders.
        </Alert>
      </Stack>

      <Stack as="section" gap="group" aria-labelledby="verify-title">
        <Prose>
          <h2 id="verify-title">5. Verify and build</h2>
          <p>
            Test the changed screens at mobile and desktop widths in both appearance modes.
            Use Tab and the arrow keys to operate the theme selector and confirm visible focus.
            Reload and move between routes to check that the chosen theme persists.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Add multiple products, remove them, and verify that the cart total returns to zero.</li>
            <li>Change the dashboard period and confirm that its metrics and chart agree.</li>
            <li>Choose each portfolio category and return to the full collection.</li>
            <li>Check long labels, enlarged text, and reduced motion after adding your content.</li>
          </ul>
        </Prose>
        <Code code={'pnpm check\npnpm build\npnpm preview'} copy label="Check and preview the production build" language="bash" variant="block" />
        <Prose>
          <p>
            Deploy the generated <code>dist/</code> directory with a host that supports static Astro
            sites. The MIT license allows personal and commercial use. Keep its copyright and license
            notice with copies or substantial portions of the starter.
          </p>
        </Prose>
        <Stack direction="horizontal" gap="related" wrap>
          <ButtonLink href="/starters/astro/dashboard" showArrow>Try the dashboard</ButtonLink>
          <ButtonLink href="/docs/frameworks/astro" variant="secondary">Read the Astro component guide</ButtonLink>
        </Stack>
      </Stack>
    </Stack>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
